  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 944 AM MDT Thu Jun 25 2026\n\nThe Heat Advisory remains in effect for El Paso and Hudspeth\nCounties along the Rio Grande until 9 PM MDT this evening.\nTemperatures will range from 103-105 for most of the lowlands\ntoday. More moisture will push into our area today, giving the\nregion a chance of isolated to scattered thunderstorms this\nafternoon and evening, with the high-terrains having the best\nchance of thunderstorms (15-25%). Some gusty outflows are possible\nwith these thunderstorms. Friday will see slightly less moisture\nin our area, but it will be sufficient enough to produce more\nshowers and thunderstorms.\n\nThe high pressure system will move east as a large upper-level \ntrough from the Pacific Northwest will push moisture out of our \narea this weekend and cool temperatures down to below 100 degrees,\nwith any remaining moisture hanging in the Sacramento Mountains\nand Hudspeth Counties, leaving a slight chance of storms (20-30%)\nSaturday and Sunday. However, this trough will bring some breezy \n(10-20 mph) winds, especially on Sunday, which will raise fire \nweather conditions to elevated and near- critical for the Gila. \nTemperatures will stay in the 90s as we enter July, but the same \nmoisture plume will stay in place due to the trough out west and \nthe high out east, raising the probability of storm chances \nmidweek.",
